<body>
<main>
<h1 id="awesome-skycd">Awesome SkyCD</h1>
<blockquote>
<p>A curated list of community plugin sources for <a href="https://github.com/SkyCD/SkyCD">SkyCD</a>.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>SkyCD plugins are distributed by their publishers as NuGet feeds described by a manifest. This list links to publisher-owned manifests; it does not host, mirror or review plugin binaries.</p>
<h2 id="contents">Contents</h2>
<ul>
{% for category in categories | sort(attribute='name', case_sensitive=false) -%}
<li><a href="#{{ category.name | lower | replace(' ', '-') }}">{{ category.name | e }}</a></li>
{% endfor -%}
</ul>
{% for category in categories | sort(attribute='name', case_sensitive=false) %}
<h2 id="{{ category.name | lower | replace(' ', '-') }}">{{ category.name | e }}</h2>
<p>{{ category.description | e }}</p>
<ul>
{% for item in category['items'] | sort(attribute='name', case_sensitive=false) -%}
<li><a href="{{ item.project_url | e }}">{{ item.name | e }}</a> - {{ item.description | e }}</li>
{% endfor -%}
</ul>
{% endfor %}
<h2 id="catalog-endpoint">Catalog endpoint</h2>
<p>Each merged change to <code>catalog.yaml</code> is published to GitHub Pages as a formatted page and as the machine-readable catalog:</p>
<pre><code>https://skycd.github.io/awesome-skycd/
https://skycd.github.io/awesome-skycd/plugins.json
</code></pre>
<p>The endpoint is public, requires no authentication, and returns a JSON array of unique absolute HTTPS URLs. Each URL points directly at a publisher-owned manifest. The directory stores no package IDs, versions or binaries. An empty array is valid.</p>
<p>Verify it from a clean client:</p>
<pre><code>curl -sS https://skycd.github.io/awesome-skycd/plugins.json
</code></pre>
<p>Format example only (not a listing):</p>
<pre><code>[
  "https://plugins.example.com/skycd/manifest.json"
]
</code></pre>
<p>Publishers own their manifests, NuGet feeds and release history. Once a source is listed, the author ships updates through those resources without changing this directory. The listing changes only when the manifest URL moves or the source is delisted.</p>
<h2 id="contributing">Contributing</h2>
<p>Read the <a href="https://github.com/SkyCD/awesome-skycd/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">contribution guide</a> for inclusion criteria, the submission and review process, source moves, removal policy and the contribution checklist. Delisting affects only this list; it never uninstalls anything from a user's machine.</p>
<p>This page is rendered from <a href="https://github.com/SkyCD/awesome-skycd/blob/main/catalog.yaml">catalog.yaml</a> by <a href="https://github.com/SkyCD/awesome-skycd/blob/main/.github/workflows/render-catalog.yml">.github/workflows/render-catalog.yml</a>. On merge, that workflow regenerates the list, renders this page and publishes <code>plugins.json</code> to GitHub Pages. Pull-request CI validates the catalog schema and renders the templates without executing plugin code.</p>
<h2 id="follow-the-work">Follow the work</h2>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://github.com/SkyCD/SkyCD/issues/801">SkyCD in-app plugin installation</a></li>
<li><a href="https://github.com/SkyCD/awesome-skycd/issues/1">Directory and contribution rules</a></li>
<li><a href="https://github.com/SkyCD/awesome-skycd/issues/2">Publisher guide and reference plugin</a></li>
</ul>
</main>
